INITIAL = """You are given a video and a query that describes the target object(s). First localize the target object(s) with one enclosing bounding box, then provide {k} discriminative points on the target object(s) and their confidence scores for every requested frame. Multiple target instances form one target set. Output one record per requested frame, in the supplied order. Coordinates and confidence are three-digit integers from 000 to 999 with leading zeros; divide them by 999 to obtain normalized values. Use the following exact structure for each frame: <BOX>x1 y1 x2 y2</BOX>; <POINTS>u1 v1 c1; ...; uK vK cK</POINTS>. Query: {query}"""

REFINE = """Check whether each previously predicted point lies on the target object(s) described by the query. Keep reliable points and replace unreliable points with better points, maintaining exactly {k} points per frame. Re-evaluate their confidence. Keep the original boxes unchanged. Output one <POINTS>u1 v1 c1; ...; uK vK cK</POINTS> record per requested frame in the supplied order. Coordinates and confidence remain three-digit integers from 000 to 999 with leading zeros. Query: {query}"""

AUXILIARY = """You are given a video, a reasoning query, and corresponding target masks. The first video shows the original RGB frames and the second shows the same frames with the target union highlighted in red. Generate exactly one additional natural-language query referring to the same target set from this alternative perspective: {perspective}. Preserve the identity and number of target objects. Output only the query. Original query: {query}"""
